From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caomengxuan666 <2507560089@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:47:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(niu): cover Niu in the unix-only shell matches and
 pin the wrapper boundary

Adding a ShellType variant only breaks builds on platforms that compile the
match. Two of them live behind #[cfg(unix)], so they never compile on the
Windows runner this port was checked on and would have failed Linux and macOS CI:

- exec-server/src/shell_snapshot.rs: the restore-flag match ended at
  `ShellType::PowerShell | ShellType::Cmd => unreachable!()`.
- exec-server/src/shell_snapshot_file.rs: the snapshot-transport match ended at
  `ShellType::Sh | ShellType::PowerShell | ShellType::Cmd => { ... }`.

Both now list Niu alongside the other unsupported shells. The audit is
believed complete rather than sampled: a match over ShellType only compiles if
it names every variant or has a wildcard arm, so enumerating every
`ShellType::Cmd` and `Self::Cmd` site finds every remaining hole. All other
sites either already had the arm or end in a wildcard.

The remaining safety question is settled by the fork's own plan doc, which says
NiuBash exposes -C instead of bash/zsh-style -lc and that Codex "should not
depend on it" until NiuBash adds it. So extract_bash_command's accepted flag set
is correct as written, and accepting a flag NiuBash rejects would be the actual
bug: the wrapped script would pass through unextracted and therefore
uninspected. Recorded that reasoning at the match and pinned it with
niu_wrapper_flags_match_the_shell_it_wraps, which asserts -C/-c/--repl-command
extract and -lc/-l/-i/--login do not.
---
 codex-rs/exec-server/src/shell_snapshot.rs    |  2 +-
 .../exec-server/src/shell_snapshot_file.rs    |  2 +-
 codex-rs/shell-command/src/bash.rs            | 29 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

